Citing its own sources, the report claims that Apple has been more cautious about shipments since early September because of the rising cost of memory chips, leading to higher prices. Component orders for October were said to have been cut by at least 15 percent compared with what was originally requested.<br/>
<br/>
The iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max start at &#36;1,199 and &#36;1,299 respectively, which is &#36;100 more than the models they replace. Apple has <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/17/apple-increasing-prices/">publicly blamed</a> AI-driven memory chip costs for the recent price increases across its lineup, which has seen prices of MacBooks and iPads tick up, as well as for <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/apple-raises-iphone-17-prices/">iPhone 16 and 17 models</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/19/apple-just-raised-more-prices/">other products</a>.<br/>
<br/>
